authorized to bind the Customer. Unless you have accepted this Agreement and hold a valid license,
you have no right to install or use the Software.

Contract documents. The contract documents are: the version of this Agreement, the Support Policy
and the Refund Policy displayed or linked before acceptance; the order confirmation; and the
supported platform versions listed in the compatibility section of the product page for the ordered
Software at the time of the order (the "compatibility specification"); statements about versions
released later are not part of it. MageMe makes these documents available with the order
confirmation. The order confirmation prevails over this Agreement only as to the product, edition,
quantity, price, licensed Production Installation and Plan term. The Support Policy and the Refund
Policy apply as far as they do not conflict with this Agreement. The website Terms of Service govern
the use of the website only and do not change a Software license. Terms in a purchase order,
procurement portal or other Customer document do not apply unless MageMe accepts them in writing.

Statements outside the contract documents. For Business Customers, other product-page content,
documentation, marketing materials and other statements are informational and do not create
warranties or contractual obligations, except where this Agreement expressly refers to them
