1. DEFINITIONS

1. License — the right to use the Software granted under this Agreement.

2. Customer, you — the legal entity or natural person identified in the order as the buyer, or the
   person to whom a license has been transferred under section 5. For free Software obtained without
   an order, Customer means the person or legal entity that installs or uses the Software. A MageMe
   account is the means through which the Customer acts; actions in the account are attributed to
   the Customer under section 3.6.

3. Consumer — a natural person who acts for purposes outside their trade, business, craft or
   profession. Business Customer — every other Customer. A natural person who buys a license for a
   store that is run as a business is a Business Customer unless the business purpose of the
   purchase is so limited that it is not predominant. This Agreement applies to every Customer; a
   provision marked for Business Customers or for Consumers applies only to them, and mandatory
   consumer law prevails where it cannot be excluded.

4. Production Installation — one live Magento installation: one Magento application using one main
   database, including all its websites, stores, store views and domains and any frontends that read
   from or write to it. All servers that together run one installation count as one installation. An
   installation is live if real customers can use it, publicly, behind a login or through an API, or
   if it processes real orders. A copy of an installation is a separate Production Installation if
   the copy is live. A separate main database is a separate Production Installation, even if it
   shares servers or code. An installation that runs stores for several businesses that are not
   under common control (majority ownership or voting rights), for example a SaaS or multi-tenant
   platform, needs one Production License per business.

5. Production License — a paid license for one Production Installation. A Production License is
   active unless it is suspended or terminated.

6. Development License — a free license for testing and development only. MageMe decides how many it
   issues, may refuse a Development License, and may revoke it immediately for breach, misuse, a
   security or legal risk, discontinuation of the product, or if the Production License it was
   issued for ends or is transferred. Mandatory rights of Consumers remain unaffected.

7. Support & Update Plan ("Plan") — the period during which you may obtain new versions of the
   Software and request support. The Plan starts on the order date and is active until its end date
   unless it is suspended. The first year of the Plan is included in the purchase. The Plan can be
   renewed at the prices and on the terms MageMe offers at the time of renewal.

8. Covered Version — a version of the licensed product and edition that MageMe has designated as
   generally available, within the Generation the license covers (section 3.5), and that MageMe
   released on or before the last day of your Plan. Pre-release builds are Covered Versions only
   where MageMe says so in writing.

9. Generation — a product line that MageMe designates as a separate generation on the product page
   before it is released. A change of the major version number alone does not make a release a
   Generation.

10. Support Policy — the support scope and channels published on the support page at the time your
   Plan starts or is renewed. Refund Policy — the refund conditions published at
   https://mageme.com/refund-policy at the time of your order.

11. Repository — MageMe's download service for Software packages. Store address — the public web
   address of the installation that the Software reports.

12. Activation — entering your license key in the Software so that MageMe's license server can
   verify the license.

2. LICENSE GRANT

1. MageMe grants you a non-exclusive license, without time limit, to use each Covered Version of the
   Software on the licensed Production Installation, subject to sections 4, 11 and 14 and the rest
   of this Agreement.

2. You may also use the Software on non-public staging, testing and development copies of the
   licensed Production Installation. These copies must not serve another project or client.

3. You may move a Production License to a new Production Installation, for example when you migrate
   the store to new hosting or rebuild it. Deactivate the license on the old installation before
   activating it on the new one. The old installation may keep the Software only for the time
   technically necessary to complete the migration, at most 30 days, and must not be operated as a
   second live installation.

4. A Development License may be used only on non-production installations and never on a live
   installation. A Development License covers a version of a Generation only if the same Customer
   holds an active Production License of the same product and edition that has received the
   Generation Upgrade to that Generation (section 3.5) and covers that version.

5. Free products. For a product that MageMe offers free of charge, MageMe grants you a non-exclusive
   license, without time limit, to use every version of that product that MageMe makes available
   free of charge on any number of installations, subject to this Agreement. Every such version is a
   Covered Version for a free product. No Plan, support or voluntary warranty is included, and
   MageMe may stop distributing or developing a free product at any time. Mandatory rights of
   Consumers remain unaffected.

6. You may modify the Software for the licensed installation and may let a contractor do this on
   your behalf; a contractor receives no rights of its own and may use the Software only for your
   licensed installation while working for you. No modification transfers or limits MageMe's rights
   in the Software; you keep the rights you lawfully own in your original additions, and MageMe has
   no obligation to support modified Software.

7. MageMe and its licensors keep all intellectual property and other rights in the Software,
   documentation, license keys and updates. All rights not expressly granted in this Agreement are
   reserved. The Software is licensed, not sold. If you send MageMe suggestions or feedback, you
   confirm that you may do so and grant MageMe a perpetual, irrevocable, worldwide, transferable,
   royalty-free license to use and exploit it without restriction or attribution.

3. SUPPORT & UPDATE PLAN AND VERSIONS

1. While your Plan is active you may download and use the generally available versions that MageMe
   makes available for your product, edition and Generation during the Plan, and you may request
   support within the Support Policy. For Business Customers, MageMe has no obligation to issue any
   particular release, feature or compatibility update, and a new version may change or remove
   features. Consumers keep their mandatory right to updates required for conformity. Nothing in
   this Agreement limits obligations to provide security updates, handle vulnerabilities or make
   notifications that mandatory law imposes on MageMe; those obligations are independent of the
   Plan.

2. When the Plan ends, you keep a license without time limit to continue using every Covered
   Version. The end of the Plan ends new versions and support; it does not end the License.
   Reinstallation and activation on a new installation require access to MageMe's license server,
   and MageMe does not guarantee that activation services remain available indefinitely (section
   14.2). Keep your own copies of the Software packages and license keys; MageMe may, but is not
   obliged to, keep earlier versions available in the Repository.

3. Versions released after your Plan ended are not covered. To use them you need to renew the Plan.
   MageMe may offer a grace period and a reduced renewal price; both are shown at checkout at the
   time of renewal and may be changed or withdrawn for future renewals. A renewal made within the
   grace period continues from the previous end date; a renewal made later starts on the renewal
   date.

4. The release date of each version is the date recorded in the Repository or, where the Repository
   has no date, in the changelog. These records may be submitted as evidence of the release date.

5. Generation Upgrade. A new Generation becomes available to an existing Production License only
   after the Customer accepts this Agreement for that license (a "Generation Upgrade"). The license
   key stays the same. Until the Generation Upgrade is accepted, the license covers only the earlier
   Generation. MageMe may offer a Generation Upgrade free of charge to some licenses, on the
   conditions it states on the product page at that time; those conditions are part of this
   Agreement for that Generation. MageMe may change or withdraw such an offer for licenses that have
   not yet accepted it. Pre-release builds included in such an offer are provided for testing only,
   may contain defects, are not supported and are not intended for live installations. Whether a
   Generation Upgrade requires a renewal is stated on the product page and in the Customer's account
   before acceptance.

6. Accepting a Generation Upgrade. A Generation Upgrade is accepted in the Customer's MageMe account
   or, where MageMe offers it, in the admin area of an installation where the license is activated.
   When a Generation Upgrade requires a renewal, access to the new Generation stays pending until
   the renewal is paid. An acceptance binds the Customer if it is made by a person with actual
   authority, by a person whose authority MageMe reasonably inferred from the Customer's own
   statements or conduct, or if the Customer later ratifies it; use of credentials or an
   installation under the Customer's control is evidence of authority. MageMe records the acceptance
   together with the data described in the Privacy Policy. The accepted text is available in the
   Customer's account while the account exists; MageMe keeps the record for the applicable
   limitation period. The accepted version of this Agreement governs the license from then on.
   Accepting a Generation Upgrade does not waive or reduce the use rights you already hold in
   Covered Versions of the earlier Generation.

7. Downloads. Packages can be downloaded from the Repository while your Plan is active. When the
   Plan ends, you keep the copies you have already downloaded and your installed Covered Versions
   keep working under section 3.2; to download a package again, renew the Plan. A Consumer may
   download again at any time the Covered Versions already obtained.

4. ACTIVATION AND LICENSE VERIFICATION

1. The Software may require activation and may periodically contact MageMe's license server to
   verify the license. MageMe may change the activation and verification methods, including for
   versions already released, for security, legal, anti-abuse or technical reasons. MageMe will not
   disable an already activated Covered Version solely because the Plan has ended.

2. If the license is not activated, if the installed version is not a Covered Version, or if the
   license is suspended or terminated, MageMe may limit functions of the Software to the extent
   reasonably necessary to enforce this Agreement. Non-excludable rights of Consumers to retrieve
   their content remain unaffected.

3. MageMe does not warrant uninterrupted verification or operation without a connection to the
   license server. Temporary unavailability of the license server may delay verification. Section
   14.2 applies if the license server is discontinued.

4. During activation and verification the Software sends MageMe the data described in the Privacy
   Policy (https://mageme.com/privacy-policy), and MageMe records requests to the Repository. MageMe
   uses this data to verify licenses, provide support, secure its services, prevent and investigate
   misuse, meet legal obligations and establish or defend legal claims, for the periods stated in
   the Privacy Policy. You must not block, alter or falsify this data.

5. You are responsible for safeguarding your account credentials and license keys and must notify
   MageMe promptly of a suspected compromise, unauthorized activation or unauthorized transfer.

5. AGENCIES AND LICENSE TRANSFER

1. An agency or developer may buy a Production License in its own name for later transfer to a
   client; it is then the Customer until the transfer. Or it may place the order as the client's
   authorized representative, naming the client as the buyer; the client is then the Customer from
   the start. An agency or developer that bought a Production License for a client's installation
   must transfer that license to the client under section 5.2 when the client asks for it after the
   agency's work for the client has ended, unless the client agrees otherwise in writing; until then
   the agency remains responsible under section 5.4.

2. Contractual transfer. A Production License may be transferred to another person through the
   transfer function of the MageMe account or by request to MageMe support. A contractual transfer
   requires that the whole license and any unexpired Plan rights are transferred together, that
   nothing is unpaid for that license, that the receiving Customer accepts this Agreement, and that
   the transferring Customer stops using the Software under that license on its own behalf and makes
   its copies unusable, except that it may continue as the new Customer's contractor under section
   2.6. MageMe may refuse a contractual transfer that does not meet these conditions or that it
   reasonably considers fraudulent, and may ask for evidence. A completed transfer under this
   section 5 is final, except to correct a mistake or fraud. MageMe is not a party to the
   arrangement between the transferring and the receiving Customer and does not resolve disputes
   between them.

3. Transfer under mandatory law. Where mandatory exhaustion law permits the resale of a Software
   copy with its unlimited use right, MageMe's consent is not required. In that case the license
   must be transferred as an indivisible whole, the transferor must make every copy in its
   possession unusable at the time of transfer, and the acquirer must provide reasonable evidence of
   lawful acquisition on request. Plan rights transfer only if the parties transfer them. The
   acquirer is bound by the restrictions of this Agreement that apply to the use of the Software.

4. The Customer is responsible for use of the Software by its employees, agencies, contractors and
   store operators as if it were its own use, and for ensuring that the installations it manages
   comply with this Agreement.

5. A universal legal successor of the Customer (for example after a merger) succeeds to the licenses
   by operation of law and must notify MageMe and update the account promptly. A buyer of assets or
   of the business may take over a license only under section 5.2 or 5.3.

6. RESTRICTIONS

You may not:

1. use one Production License on more than one live Production Installation at the same time, except
   as section 2.3 permits during a migration, or hold fewer active Production Licenses (section 1.5)
   for a product than the number of live Production Installations on which that product is used at
   any time;

2. use a Development License on a live installation;

3. install, activate or use a version of the Software that is not a Covered Version for your
   license, including a version released after your Plan ended, unless you first renew the Plan;

4. sell, sublicense, rent or lend the Software, or provide the Software itself, its source code or
   administrative access to it to third parties as a hosted or standalone product, or include the
   Software, modified or not, in a product, theme, package or service that you sell, license or host
   for third parties, except by transferring a license under section 5; operating a Production
   Installation licensed as required by section 1.4 is permitted, and so is access by your personnel
   and contractors under section 2.6;

5. publish the source code of the Software (except stylesheets, JavaScript and images delivered to
   the browser, and third-party components whose own license requires source availability) or place
   it in a publicly accessible repository;

6. remove, hide or alter copyright, license or ownership notices in the Software, including notices
   in file and class names, code comments and the admin interface;

7. circumvent, disable, falsify or conceal information from license activation or verification, or
   help anyone else to do so, except to the limited extent that applicable law grants a right that
   cannot be excluded;

8. reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the Software or derive its non-public protocols or
   structure from it, except to the extent that applicable law grants a right that cannot be
   excluded;

9. copy or use MageMe's source code, protected expression or trade secrets to create or distribute
   competing software, or use MageMe's name or trademarks without written permission; this does not
   restrict independently created software or lawful competition.

7. UNAUTHORIZED USE AND COMPLIANCE

1. If MageMe finds that the Software is used in breach of this Agreement, MageMe gives you at least
   15 days to remedy the breach and, pending clarification, may apply proportionate temporary
   restrictions. No remedy period is required where the breach cannot be remedied or involves
   deliberate circumvention of activation or verification, distribution or publication of the
   Software or its source code, fraud, a sanctions breach, an immediate material security threat to
   MageMe's services, or repeated breach; in these cases MageMe may suspend or terminate the
   affected licenses, downloads or support immediately, and may restrict the whole account where the
   breach, fraud, sanctions issue or security threat affects the account as a whole. MageMe states
   the general basis of a restriction where disclosure is lawful and does not compromise security or
   enforcement, and may maintain it while its grounds continue.

2. For proven unauthorized use, you owe MageMe the license or renewal fee applicable to the
   identified installations and the actual periods of unauthorized use, statutory interest from the
   date a quantified amount became due, enforcement costs recoverable under law, and any further
   loss MageMe can prove, without double recovery. For use of a version that is not a Covered
   Version, the fee is the renewal fee that would have covered the versions used, calculated under
   section 3.3 as if the Plan had been renewed on the date the unauthorized use began, at the list
   renewal price without grace discount. Payment of these fees does not create a license for the
   past or the future unless MageMe says so in writing. A Consumer is liable only to the extent
   permitted by mandatory law.

3. On MageMe's written request with reasonable grounds, a Business Customer provides within 14 days
   a list of the installations where the Software is used and a written confirmation of compliance.
   If these do not resolve the concern, an independent auditor bound by confidentiality may verify
   compliance, on at least 10 business days' notice, during business hours, no more than once in 12
   months unless material under-licensing is found, and limited to records and systems needed to
   verify licensing. MageMe bears the cost of the audit unless it finds material under-licensing, in
   which case the Business Customer pays the documented reasonable costs. Under-licensing is
   material if it requires at least one additional Production License or Plan renewal.

4. A Business Customer will indemnify MageMe against third-party claims, final awards and reasonable
   defence costs arising from the Customer's culpable breach of this Agreement, unlawful content,
   unlawful use of the Software, a modification not supplied by MageMe, or the data the Customer
   collects or processes with the Software, except to the extent caused by MageMe. MageMe notifies
   the Customer promptly, lets the Customer control the defence with competent counsel, cooperates
   reasonably and does not settle in a way that imposes liability or admissions on the Customer
   without the Customer's consent.

5. Other rights and remedies under applicable law, including injunctive relief, remain unaffected.

