11. TERMINATION

1. MageMe may terminate a license by written notice if you materially breach this Agreement and do
   not remedy the breach within the period given under section 7.1, or immediately in the cases
   listed in section 7.1 for which no remedy period is required. MageMe may terminate all licenses
   of a Customer for repeated breach or for a breach listed in section 7.1 for which no remedy
   period is required.

2. After termination you must stop using the Software under the terminated license on all
   installations, remove it, delete the license key, make all usable copies unusable, and make sure
   your contractors do the same. Copies contained in backups that cannot reasonably be isolated must
   stay inaccessible, must never be restored or used, and must be deleted through your ordinary
   backup retention cycle. On request you confirm compliance in writing. MageMe may disable the
   license key and deny downloads and support. A Business Customer that continues to use the
   Software after termination bears MageMe's reasonable costs of enforcement to the extent
   recoverable under applicable law.

3. Your data stays in your installation; termination gives MageMe no access to it. After termination
   MageMe may limit functions of the Software under section 4.2. A terminated license does not
   permit storefront or other operational use.

4. The end of a Plan is not a termination; section 3.2 applies.

5. A valid termination by MageMe for your breach does not create a refund right. No refund is due
   under the Refund Policy for a license that was used in a material breach of this Agreement that
   is not cured under section 7.1, or where you are in such a breach at the time of the request;
   this does not affect a Consumer's right of withdrawal or statutory remedies. This does not
   exclude rights arising from MageMe's own breach or from mandatory law.

6. Sections 1, 2.7, 3.4, 6, 7.2 to 7.5, 8.3 to 8.7, 9, 10.3, 11.2, 11.3, 11.5, 13, 14.3 and 15, the
   ownership rules of section 2.6, and accrued payment obligations remain in force after
   termination. The record-keeping and legal-claims provisions of section 4.4 survive for the period
   and purposes permitted by data protection law and the Privacy Policy. Support rights do not
   survive termination or the end of the Plan.

12. RIGHT OF WITHDRAWAL (CONSUMERS)

If the mandatory law applicable to your contract gives you a right of withdrawal as a Consumer, its
