   arising after conclusion of the contract that MageMe could not reasonably prevent, avoid or
   overcome, such as infrastructure or supplier outages, cyberattacks, governmental action, natural
   disaster, or serious illness or incapacity of key personnel, where the event meets that test. The
   excuse lasts while the impediment continues. Mandatory consumer rights remain unaffected.

2. Payments. Prices for Business Customers exclude VAT and other taxes unless stated otherwise;
   Consumers pay the total price shown before ordering. Business Customers pay without set-off or
   deduction except where mandatory law provides otherwise. An unpaid amount, a failed payment, or a
   payment reversal not finally upheld by the payment provider, a court or applicable law is treated
   as non-payment. MageMe may suspend the item or service for which payment is outstanding after
   notice until payment is settled; a Production License is suspended only where the outstanding
   amount is the initial price of that license, and non-payment of an optional Plan renewal does not
   affect the right to use existing Covered Versions. If a discount or special offer was granted on
   conditions that you did not meet, MageMe notifies you; a Business Customer then chooses within 14
   days between cancellation of the affected order with a refund of the amount paid and an invoice
   for the difference to the price without the discount; a Consumer is offered the refund only.

3. Confidentiality. A Business Customer protects the non-public source code, license keys and
   technical materials of the Software with at least reasonable care and discloses them only to
   personnel and contractors who need them for licensed use and are bound by equivalent
   confidentiality duties.

4. Assignment. You may not assign this Agreement or a license except as described in section 5. You
   consent in advance to MageMe transferring this Agreement, a license or any related rights and
   obligations to any third party upon notice to you, provided the transfer does not reduce a non-
   excludable Consumer right.

5. Third-party components. Components identified in the notices delivered with the Software are
   governed by their own open-source or third-party licenses. MageMe gives Business Customers no
   additional warranty for those components.

6. Export and sanctions. You must not export, supply or use the Software in breach of applicable
   export-control or sanctions laws, or allow a prohibited person to use it. You confirm that you
   are not a prohibited person.

7. Entire agreement. The contract documents are the whole agreement about the license. They replace
   earlier agreements about the same license and any license text shipped inside a Software package,
   except as section 10.1 provides and except the third-party licenses in section 15.5. A Business
   Customer confirms that it has not relied on any statement outside the contract documents, other
   than an expressly designated written warranty; this does not exclude liability for intentional
   conduct, gross negligence, deliberate concealment, or a statement that applicable law makes
   binding.

8. Severability and waiver. If a provision is found invalid or unenforceable, it is severed to the
   extent necessary and the rest of the Agreement stays in force. For Business Customers, the
   invalid provision is replaced by the valid provision that comes closest to its purpose, as far as
   applicable law permits. A provision that is invalid for Consumers remains valid for Business
   Customers. A delay in enforcing a right is not a waiver of that right.

9. Relationship and third parties. The parties are independent contractors. This Agreement creates
   no rights for third parties.

10. Language. For Business Customers, this Agreement is concluded in English and the English text
   prevails over any translation. Consumers receive the language version required by applicable law.
